# t55: the numeric-or-raise binop rule (#65 inc. 2). Ops the VM defines only
# for numbers (- * / % & | ^ << >>) are claimed numeric regardless of operand
# classification, so accumulators whose RHS reads a boxed name (a for-in loop
# var, an env-boxed list element, a boxed `len of`) stay native C doubles
# instead of demoting to env storage — the spec_audit top finding (crc32's c).
# Boxed operands emit through CHECKED reads (aot_num_ck: loud exactly where
# the VM raises, never a silent 0.0). `+` is numeric when EITHER side is
# provably numeric (str+str still concatenates elsewhere); and/or with both
# sides numeric return the OPERAND with short-circuit.

# for-in cascade: acc reads the boxed loop var through * and +
acc is 0
for v in range of 10:
    acc is acc + (v * 3)
print of acc

# env-boxed list element in arithmetic (the crc32 table shape)
tbl is [5, 10, 15, 20]
c is 7
i is 0
loop while i < 4:
    c is (c * 2) ^ tbl[i]
    i is i + 1
print of c

# boxed len in arithmetic (the t45 regression shape: len of a LIST, not a
# buffer, must route through the boxed call, not aot_buf_len)
xs is [10, 20, 30]
print of (len of xs - 1)
print of ((len of xs) * (len of xs) + 1)

# numeric and/or return the operand and short-circuit
a is 3
b is 0
print of (a and 5)
print of (b and 5)
print of (b or 9)
print of (a or 9)
mix is (a and b) or (a * 2)
print of mix

# `+` with one provably numeric side over a boxed read
s is 0
for w in range of 5:
    s is s + w
print of s

# string + string still concatenates (the + rule must not claim this)
greet is "gen" + "eric"
print of greet
